           <li>{{ city }}: {{ items|map(attribute="name")|join(", ") }}</li>
         {% endfor %}</ul>
 
+    Groups are sorted in ascending order of the attribute value by
+    default. Pass ``reverse=true`` to sort the groups in descending
+    order instead.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        <ul>{% for year, items in posts|groupby("year", reverse=true) %}
+          <li>{{ year }}: {{ items|map(attribute="title")|join(", ") }}</li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
+    You can specify a ``key_transform`` callable to change how each
+    group key is displayed, for example to format a date. It is applied
+    to the key of each group after the items have been grouped, so it
+    only changes the ``grouper`` value of the result and never how the
+    items are sorted or grouped.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        <ul>{% for month, items in posts|groupby("date", key_transform=month_format) %}
+          <li>{{ month }}: {{ items|map(attribute="title")|join(", ") }}</li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.1
+        Added the ``key_transform`` parameter.
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.1
+        Added the ``reverse`` parameter.
+
     .. versionchanged:: 3.0
         Added the ``default`` parameter.
 
